Subject: [PATCH] irqchip: mask inherited P4 CLIC slots before mapping

On the Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6 with P4 silicon v1.3, the IDF loader leaves
CLIC slot 18 enabled and selectively vectored for its SYSTIMER interrupt.
The UP driver reuses that slot for UART0, routing the new source before
replacing the IDF vector attributes and before request_irq installs the
Linux handler. An assertion in that window can enter the retained IDF
vector.

Mask the slot before changing its route or attributes. Linux IRQ startup
owns re-enabling it during protected action setup. With the other images
and configuration unchanged, three EN resets reached the shell on
the first attempt instead of entering the IDF recursive-panic path and
recovering through a software reset.

This patch is for the UP irqchip implementation. The C68 SMP routing patch
has a separate map implementation and is left unchanged.

--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-esp32p4-clic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-esp32p4-clic.c
@@ -103,6 +103,12 @@
 	u8 attr;
 	irq_flow_handler_t handler;
 
+	/*
+	 * The loader may leave this slot enabled with an IDF vector. Mask it
+	 * before routing the new source; Linux unmasks it once a handler is ready.
+	 */
+	writeb(0, clic_base + hwirq * 4 + CLIC_INTIE_OFF);
+
 	if (clic_intmtx_base && clic_intmtx_source[hwirq])
 		writel(hwirq, clic_intmtx_base + clic_intmtx_source[hwirq] * 4);
 
